# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback.
#
# Dashboard sections are real URLs (/dashboard/portfolio, /dashboard/trades, …)
# handled client-side by React Router. A hard load or refresh of one of those
# paths must return the app shell with a 200, not a 404.
#
# Ordering matters: Cloudflare Pages runs Pages Functions (functions/api/**)
# BEFORE this file, and serves an existing static asset (anything in dist/)
# before falling through to these rewrites. So a request is only ever rewritten
# by the catch-all below when it is a non-asset, non-Function path — exactly the
# client-side routes. In particular /api/* is answered by its Function and never
# reaches this rule, so no API call can be rewritten to the HTML shell.

/*  /index.html  200
